### KnowledgeBase stack configuration TEMPLATE — copy to .env (gitignored):
###   cp .env.template .env   (or run `make bootstrap`, which does it for you)
### .env.template is the tracked config of record (NO secrets). .env is gitignored.
### The only stack secret is WEBUI_SECRET_KEY (in .env.local, gitignored). Run
### `make bootstrap` once to create .env.local and the ./data tree. Agents
### authenticate with KB_API_KEY (an Open WebUI per-account key — not stored here;
### provisioned via the api-gateway admin endpoint, see README).

# api-gateway run user (auto-set by `make bootstrap` from id -u/id -g; no
# default in compose; override if the ./gdrive owner uid:gid differs from login)
HOST_UID=
HOST_GID=

# ---- Data root (bind-mount source). Keep ./data to store on the SSD; later
# ---- move ./data to RAID and symlink it back: ./data -> /mnt/RAID/kb/data
DATA_ROOT=./data

# ---- Ollama (EXTERNAL). OLLAMA_HOST is Ollama's native client env var: the
# ---- full URL of the Ollama host (scheme + host + port). REQUIRED at compose
# ---- time: there is NO host.docker.internal fallback, so `make start`/`make
# ---- config` fail fast if it is unset. Define it in your shell env, or
# ---- uncomment the line below and set it.
# ---- localhost is allowed: graphiti + markitdown-ocr run a container
# ---- entrypoint shim (scripts/ollama-host.sh) that rewrites localhost/127.0.0.1
# ---- -> host.docker.internal before the app reads it (compose adds
# ---- extra_hosts: host-gateway, so host.docker.internal reaches the Docker
# ---- host inside the container). Open WebUI persists rag.ollama.base_url to
# ---- its DB on first boot and uses the DB thereafter, so `make rag-config`
# ---- (part of `make provision`) writes the translated value to that DB; it
# ---- does NOT use the shim. For a remote/LAN GPU host, use
# ---- http://<ollama-host>:11434 as-is (the shim leaves non-localhost URLs
# ---- unchanged). The compose file appends /v1 for the OpenAI-compatible
# ---- LLM/embedder endpoints.
#OLLAMA_HOST=

# ---- Image tags
NEO4J_IMAGE_TAG=5.26.0

# graphiti REST server (graph_service). bootstrap.py injects
# OpenAIGenericClient (json_schema structured outputs, the >= 0.29 default)
# so Ollama extraction works. See graphiti/bootstrap.py.
GRAPHITI_IMAGE_TAG=0.29.3

# Custom OWUI overlay image (official OWUI + path-aware dedup-hash patch +
# upload-idempotency patch + source-mtime patch + orphan-vector-cleanup-on-
# delete patch), built locally from open-webui/. See open-webui/PATCH.md. To
# revert to the stock image, set this to `main` and remove the openwebui
# `build:` block in compose.yml. To run only the dedup patch (no
# idempotency/mtime/orphanclean), set this to `0.11.0-pathdedup`.
OPENWEBUI_IMAGE_TAG=0.11.0-pathdedup-idem-mtime-orphanclean

# ---- Host port mapping (only this one is exposed on 0.0.0.0). Caddy is the
# ---- single public edge (KB_HOST): OWUI root landing + /memory/* gateway.
# ---- Default 3000 = OWUI's natural port; Caddy listens internally on the
# ---- same port (no 3000->8000 translation). graphiti/neo4j are internal-only.
KB_HOST_PORT=3000

# Public URL agents/clients point at (KB_HOST). Caddy on KB_HOST_PORT fronts
# OWUI (/) and api-gateway (/memory/*, /admin/users, /health); agents send
# KB_API_KEY for the gateway. Use HTTPS or a VPN/tunnel for non-local access
# (KB_API_KEY is a bearer) — see README "KB_API_KEY". Deployment-specific: set
# KB_HOST in your shell env (`export KB_HOST=http://<host>:3000`) so the shell
# value overrides; uncomment + set here only if you prefer .env. Defaults to
# http://localhost:3000 when unset (scripts fall back to KB_HOST_PORT).
#KB_HOST=http://localhost:3000
# Email domain for accounts provisioned by `make bootstrap` / `make api-keys`:
# the first (admin) user is admin@<KB_DOMAIN> and the agent user is
# agent@<KB_DOMAIN>. `make bootstrap` writes admin@<KB_DOMAIN> +
# a generated password into .env.local (OPENWEBUI_FIRST_USER/PASSWORD).
# Override for a single run with `make bootstrap KB_DOMAIN=<domain>` (wins over
# this value), or set it here once for a persistent custom domain. Changing it
# here does NOT update an existing .env.local on its own: run
# `make clean-all && make bootstrap` to recompute the admin email, or edit
# .env.local by hand.
KB_DOMAIN=local.test

# api-gateway max concurrent in-flight requests (ThreadingHTTPServer semaphore).
KB_MAX_CONCURRENCY=16

# ---- Neo4j (container-network only; not published)
NEO4J_USER=neo4j
NEO4J_PASSWORD=password
NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j
NEO4J_HEAP_INITIAL=512m
NEO4J_HEAP_MAX=1G
NEO4J_PAGECACHE=512m
# graphiti -> neo4j bolt URI (internal docker network; no default in compose)
NEO4J_URI=bolt://neo4j:7687

# ---- Graphiti REST server (graphiti/bootstrap.py reads these via compose)
# graphiti_core extraction concurrency; the REST server reads nothing else
# from this section (LLM/embedder config is set in compose.yml).
SEMAPHORE_LIMIT=3

# ---- LLM model
# Two INDEPENDENT runtime models (defaults equal only so one 14B instance fits
# the ~22.5 GB GPU; you may set them differently):
#   GRAPHITI_MODEL  - Graphiti 0.29.3 extraction LLM. compose maps it to the
#                     graphiti container's native MODEL_NAME var.
#   OPENWEBUI_MODEL - OWUI chat model; the api-gateway inserts it for
#                     POST /memory/rag. `make api-keys` grants the agent read.
# Both MUST be NON-REASONING. Graphiti extraction calls GRAPHITI_MODEL with
# max_tokens=16384 and json_schema structured output; a reasoning model
# (one with a thinking chain) spends the budget on its thinking and emits
# no content (finish_reason=length) -> json.loads('') -> extraction silently
# fails. qwen2.5:14b-ctx8192 is non-reasoning and tested reliable.
#
# Context window: the /v1 endpoint ignores options.num_ctx in the request,
# so OLLAMA_MODEL_CONTEXT is baked into GRAPHITI_MODEL via a Modelfile
# (PARAMETER num_ctx) at `make pull-models` (reference: Modelfile_qwen2_5;
# see docs/operations.md#custom-model-ctx-baked-variant). The remote GPU host has ~22.5 GB
# VRAM; the stock 14B at the default 32k context loads ~53 GB and spills to
# CPU (extraction crawls). num_ctx 8192 loads ~20 GB, fits the GPU (a fact is
# searchable in ~9 s warm; a cold first load adds ~30 s model load). 8192
# covers Graphiti's prompt+schema overhead + a RAG
# conversation; raise to 16384 only if a measured canary needs it (KV cache
# scales with context and concurrency: SEMAPHORE_LIMIT=3 and host
# OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL multiply it).
# OLLAMA_MODEL_BASE is the stock build base (pulled from the registry and
# FROM'd by the Modelfile); it is NOT a runtime model.
OLLAMA_MODEL_BASE=qwen2.5:14b
OLLAMA_MODEL_CONTEXT=8192
GRAPHITI_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b-ctx8192

# OWUI chat model (the api-gateway inserts it for /memory/rag). INDEPENDENT from
# GRAPHITI_MODEL: defaults are equal so one 14B instance loads on the GPU, but
# they may differ. Two different 14B tags cannot both be resident at once on
# this GPU. .env values are literal (no ${} expansion in docker-compose), so
# when you rename a tag, run `make pull-models` (recreates GRAPHITI_MODEL) and
# ensure the OPENWEBUI_MODEL tag is pulled.
OPENWEBUI_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b-ctx8192

# ---- Embedder (MUST exist in the host Ollama: `ollama pull nomic-embed-text`)
EMBEDDER_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
EMBEDDER_DIMENSIONS=768

# ---- Open WebUI
# First registrant becomes admin (no admin creds in env). ENABLE_SIGNUP=true
# for initial bootstrap; set to false after the admin registers for a closed
# instance, then `make restart`. DEFAULT_USER_ROLE=pending means later signups
# need admin approval.
ENV=dev
ENABLE_SIGNUP=true
DEFAULT_USER_ROLE=pending

# Enable per-user API keys (for agent REST access). Flipped live by `make
# api-keys` via the admin config API; also set here so a fresh first boot
# persists the enabled state. See README "API keys & agent access".
ENABLE_API_KEYS=true

# Allow non-admin (user-role) accounts to hold API keys. Required so the
# dedicated agent user (OPENWEBUI_USER) can use its read-scoped key.
USER_PERMISSIONS_FEATURES_API_KEYS=true
RAG_EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# ---- markitdown-ocr external extraction engine (COMPOSE_PROFILES=ocr)
# OCR_ENABLED (default true) is the source of truth, decided at provision time.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES is DERIVED from it by `make bootstrap` (force-synced every
# bootstrap; non-editable) and read by `docker compose` from .env for EVERY
# command, so the ocr sidecar is always in the project when enabled -- no
# --profile flag, no shell export, no per-command toggle. When true, OCR is a
# prereq provisioned by the standard chain: `make bootstrap` generates
# OCR_SERVICE_TOKEN + bakes COMPOSE_PROFILES=ocr, `make pull-models` pulls
# OCR_MODEL, `make start` builds + starts the sidecar (via COMPOSE_PROFILES=ocr
# in .env), and `make api-keys` points OWUI at it. OWUI then routes EVERY ingest
# to markitdown-ocr (global + no per-type fallback; an empty result orphans).
# To disable OCR: `make clean-all && make provision OCR_ENABLED=false` (make
# bootstrap persists OCR_ENABLED=false + an empty COMPOSE_PROFILES into .env;
# wipes .env.local + ./data). An existing .env without OCR_ENABLED defaults to
# true. A `make provision OCR_ENABLED=<val>` override DEFINES the profile
# durably (it is persisted to .env, not a transient per-run toggle).
# OCR_SERVICE_TOKEN is a SECRET -> .env.local only (generated by `make
# bootstrap` when OCR_ENABLED=true; never commit it).
OCR_ENABLED=true
COMPOSE_PROFILES=ocr
OCR_MODEL=deepseek-ocr
OCR_PROMPT="Extract all text from this image. Return ONLY the extracted text, maintaining the original layout and order. Do not add any commentary or description."
OCR_MIN_DIM=64
OCR_TIMEOUT=120
OCR_KEEP_ALIVE=5m

# Log level for the local containers using standard `logging`
# (markitdown-ocr, kb-api-gateway, kb-graphiti). DEBUG raises third-party
# (markitdown/uvicorn) verbosity. A change needs `up -d --force-recreate`.
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ---- Open WebUI attack-surface reduction
# Tools/Skills: no workspace access and no importing (no uploading arbitrary
# Python functions). Direct tool/MCP servers off. Web search off. OpenAI
# passthrough proxy off (Open WebUI talks to Ollama only). Community sharing
# and evaluation arenas off. These are defaults for new users; an admin can
# still grant Tools/Skills access per user/group via the UI if needed later.
USER_PERMISSIONS_WORKSPACE_TOOLS_ACCESS=False
USER_PERMISSIONS_WORKSPACE_TOOLS_IMPORT=False
USER_PERMISSIONS_WORKSPACE_SKILLS_ACCESS=False
USER_PERMISSIONS_WORKSPACE_SKILLS_IMPORT=False
USER_PERMISSIONS_FEATURES_DIRECT_TOOL_SERVERS=False
USER_PERMISSIONS_FEATURES_WEB_SEARCH=False
ENABLE_OPENAI_API=False
ENABLE_WEB_SEARCH=False
ENABLE_COMMUNITY_SHARING=False
ENABLE_EVALUATION_ARENA_MODELS=False

# ---- Phone-home / outbound hardening (no host mods; compose-only)
# Open WebUI update check pings api.github.com on startup; disabled here.
ENABLE_VERSION_UPDATE_CHECK=False

# OpenTelemetry exporter (defaults to localhost:4317; off by default). Off.
ENABLE_OTEL=False

# Serve the favicon from Open WebUI itself (bind-mounted from ./docs) instead
# of the default https://openwebui.com/favicon.png. The compose file mounts
# ./docs/xgensilicon.{png,ico} over the build-source favicons so the startup
# static sync copies them into /static/. No outbound favicon fetch.
WEBUI_FAVICON_URL=/static/favicon.png

# Graphiti telemetry (phones home to us.i.posthog.com) is already off via
# GRAPHITI_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false in compose.yml.
# HuggingFace (huggingface.co) is left reachable: it is a functional
# tokenizer/embedder download (tiktoken cl100k_base), not telemetry.

# ---- gdrive index (api-gateway, stateless; no sidecar)
# PREREQ: the rclone `gdrive` remote must be configured + authenticated first
#  (one-time: `rclone config` -> new `gdrive` remote -> Google Drive storage ->
#  OAuth browser login). `make gdrive-sync` fail-fasts if no shared drives are
#  visible through the remote. Re-login only if the token expires / access is
#  revoked. Override the remote name with `gdrive-sync --remote NAME`.
#  Full setup (headless auth, verify, re-auth): see docs/gdrive.md.
# `make gdrive-sync` runs rclone (sync ./gdrive from the gdrive remote) then
# POSTs /index to api-gateway, which walks ./gdrive read-only and drives OWUI's
# native sync/diff protocol to reconcile the tree into the "gdrive" KB
# (incremental: added/modified/deleted only). `make gdrive-index` runs POST
# /index alone (set INDEX_ALL=1 for a full re-index; RETRY_PENDING=1
# re-triggers stalled pending). `make gdrive-status`
# reads GET /status. Indexing is manual/on-demand only: no daemon, no schedule.
# GDRIVE_KB_ID is NOT set by hand: `make gdrive-index-bootstrap` creates the KB,
# grants the agent user read, and writes GDRIVE_KB_ID into .env.local.
# OPENWEBUI_ADMIN_API_KEY (a SECRET, in .env.local from `make api-keys`) is
# injected into api-gateway and used for the OWUI sync writes; the caller's
# KB_API_KEY is authorization only. See docs/operations.md.
# api-gateway runs as HOST_UID/HOST_GID (set at the top of this file) so the
# owner-only ./gdrive bind mount is readable by the container.
# Max file size for the gateway source walk (strings like 100mb, 2gb). Files
# over this are skipped. The documents-only allowlist is hardcoded in
# gateway/app.py DEFAULT_ALLOW (source code is handled by open-codebase-index).
KB_MAX_SIZE=100mb

# /index + /status sync-protocol call timeout (sync/diff, dirs/create,
# sync/cleanup, list files, delete file, paginated GET /files/ status scan), in
# seconds. The 15s identity timeout is too short for a large manifest diff, a
# 159-file status scan, or a drained cleanup. Bump for a huge tree.
OWUI_INDEX_TIMEOUT=300

# markitdown-ocr image tag (sidecar; COMPOSE_PROFILES=ocr). Built locally from
# markitdown/. Built + started by `make start` when OCR_ENABLED=true; OWUI
# routing set by `make api-keys` (re-assert: `make ocr-config`). See
# docs/operations.md.
MARKITDOWN_OCR_IMAGE_TAG=0.1.1-ollama-native
